  "note": "Triennial election of the Dromore Urban Council, polled Friday 15 May 1936. Only seven nominations were received for the nine seats, so the seven were returned unopposed and two seats remained to be filled (Dromore Leader, 9 May 1936, p. 2). It was over ten years since a contest had taken place; Mr. James P. Graham was the only newcomer. Returned unopposed."
